["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Peter Galison &amp; Sophie Ritson on Imaging the Invisible clean Bayesian / forward methods mechanical objectivity tacit knowledge photon ring\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-11-thehpspodcastc-黑洞照片不是拍出来的-是四个互不通气的团队算出来的/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/588cad575b4d6366-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">45:39</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">The HPS Podcast - Conversations from History, Philosophy and Social Studies of Science</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0911</span></div>\n<h2>黑洞照片不是拍出来的，是四个互不通气的团队算出来的</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">2019 年那张 M87 黑洞照片，四个图像团队被隔离作业、互相欺骗，用 Frosty the Snowman 当测试图，只为证明他们没把想看到的东西算进数据里。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>9</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">科学哲学</span><span class=\"tag\">黑洞成像</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-core=\"1\" data-hay=\"Did Numerical Control De-skill Machinists? Numerical Control (NC) CNC journeyman agentic\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-asianometry-数控机床没让技工降级-平均技能水平几乎没变/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/d0a71dde8bc0fbd1-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">21:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>数控机床没让技工降级，平均技能水平几乎没变</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">从 1950 年代起，人们就担心数控会让机加工技工去技能化。但 A 级技工和 NC 操作工的时薪几乎持平，三十年里整体技能水平只降了约 1%。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">自动化</span><span class=\"tag\">制造业</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-core=\"1\" data-hay=\"Nathan Goes to China #3: US-China Relations, the Art of the AI Deal &amp; the Road to Pax Robotica Pax Robotica eternal 1991 cope confidential computing formal methods system three thinking\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-cogrev-出口管制的理由一路退守-只剩一个前提说得通/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b0be259c3ffba6c1-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">3:17:07</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>出口管制的理由一路退守，只剩一个前提说得通</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">最初是防军事用途，后来退成阻止前沿模型，再退成限制中国能跑多少 AI agent；这套政策唯一自洽的前提，是相信短期冲刺神级超级智能、谁先到谁通吃。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">中美关系</span><span class=\"tag\">AI 政策</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"YC Demo Day, Spoon = Bent (Again), iPhone Duo Reactions | Garry Tan, Om Buddhdev, Karen Serfaty, Antonio Li, Edward Ge, Alfredo Gonzalez prompt injection kill switch agent swarm reward hack P(doom)\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-tbpn-有人拿-1000-万美元赌-ai-不会在-2030-年前灭绝人类/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/d5c9897d5e90ae69-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:27:55</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">TBPN</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>有人拿 1000 万美元赌 AI 不会在 2030 年前灭绝人类</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">把「P(doom)」这种没法证伪的数字，换成有截止日期、能结算的命题，是这集最好用的一招：末日概率好传播，有用的却是能逐条追踪、能逐条推翻的事件链。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI 安全</span><span class=\"tag\">数据标注</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"Psychoactive substances helped spur Andean civilization, and breaking barriers to education structured pedagogy teaching at the right level implementation science learning poverty iawasa\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-sciencepod-致幻植物塑造了安第斯文明-而不只是印加人的啤酒/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/de66276d50c998a0-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">33:12</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Science Magazine Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>致幻植物塑造了安第斯文明，而不只是印加人的啤酒</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">考古学家在秘鲁和玻利维亚的骨管、鼻吸托盘和陶杯里验出了 DMT 与维拉，说明致幻药物曾是前印加复杂社会共有的信仰基础设施——而印加人转向了喝奇恰啤酒。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>11</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">考古</span><span class=\"tag\">致幻剂</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Hydrodynamic and dusty instabilities in planet formation - Min-Kai Lin VSI (vertical shear instability) COS (convective overstability) streaming instability zonal flow Stokes number resonant drag instability\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-instituteforad-行星形成靠的是尘埃自己塌缩-不是气体湍流/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7a390bde2cd3d09c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">1:00:13</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">InstituteForAdvancedStudy</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>行星形成靠的是尘埃自己塌缩，不是气体湍流</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">VSI 和 COS 这类纯流体不稳定性把尘埃搅回大气层，造不出星子；只有让尘埃主动反馈、甚至让气体吸积，才能把尘埃压到塌缩密度。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">行星形成</span><span class=\"tag\">原行星盘</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"One resignation turned the embers of AI fear into a wildfire RSI Lossy self-improvement Fast Takeoff\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-interconnects-一次辞职点燃了-ai-恐慌-但恐慌的剧本是错的/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/117435d411031fe3-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">10:59</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Interconnects</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>一次辞职点燃了 AI 恐慌，但恐慌的剧本是错的</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI 风险讨论被一次辞职推到了极端，但真正该担心的不是灭绝，而是实验室连自己的基础设施都没加固。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI 安全</span><span class=\"tag\">开放模型</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-core=\"1\" data-hay=\"Why the intelligence explosion can&#x27;t happen inside a data centre | Tom Reed sample efficiency Goodhart Singularity jaggedness continual learning RL environments\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-eightythousand-数据中心里造不出超级智能-瓶颈是真实世界的信号/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cd24910e04834e0f-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"8\"><span class=\"dur\">22:10</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">80,000 Hours</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>数据中心里造不出超级智能：瓶颈是真实世界的信号</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">把 AI 研发自动化不等于超级智能：Tom Reed 认为多数任务的数据只能在真实市场里部署模型才产生，样本效率和模拟都补不上，奇点卡在信号而非算力。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AGI 时间线</span><span class=\"tag\">数据</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Nilanjan Das on Buddhist Philosophy and Caste varnas jatis universals epistemic seeing eliminativism\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-phibites-婆罗门身份不是狗性-一位佛教哲学家如何拆掉种姓的形而上学/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/243c92b44ec40dbb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">20:37</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Philosophy Bites</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>婆罗门身份不是狗性：一位佛教哲学家如何拆掉种姓的形而上学</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">法称不否认狗有「狗性」这种共相，却拒绝承认存在「婆罗门性」——因为婆罗门与首陀罗在身体、智力、能力上没有任何可感知的差别，种姓不产生任何因果效力。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">印度哲学</span><span class=\"tag\">佛教</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"The First Space Elevator: Where Would We Build It? Earthport skyhook Lagrange points geostationary orbit mass driver\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-isaacarthur-第一座太空电梯不该建在陆地-而该建在赤道太平洋的船上/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/d168afeb223cb246-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">22:57</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">IsaacArthur</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>第一座太空电梯不该建在陆地，而该建在赤道太平洋的船上</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">第一座太空电梯选址的核心不是离城市近，而是让失败后果最小：赤道太平洋的移动海上平台，天气温和、远离航线、出事只掉进公海。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">太空电梯</span><span class=\"tag\">轨道运输</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"The Lotus Eaters Episode 7: Lying Odysseus [unlocked] xenia theodicy liminal\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-verybad-奥德修斯回到伊萨卡却不敢认自己-他撒谎是在躲什么/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/5c06d20471805861-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"V\"><span class=\"dur\">55:41</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Very Bad Wizards</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>奥德修斯回到伊萨卡却不敢认自己：他撒谎是在躲什么</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">他明明已经踏上故乡，却先编造一个克里特人的身份，连对最忠诚的猪倌也不肯说真话——因为真正的问题不是能不能回家，而是他还能不能认出自己。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">荷马</span><span class=\"tag\">奥德赛</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"When AI Improves Itself | Richard Socher (Recursive) recursive self-improvement next-token prediction Jevons paradox virtual cell open-endedness\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-madpod-ai-自我改进的瓶颈不是算力-是模拟与验证/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/90800bca4b008abf-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:14:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">MAD Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>AI 自我改进的瓶颈不是算力，是模拟与验证</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">凡是能被模拟的领域，AI 终将解决；凡是无法模拟的领域，再强的模型也只能等实验数据。Richard Socher 认为递归自我改进的路径是先让 AI 研究 AI，再攻生物。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>10</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI for Science</span><span class=\"tag\">递归自我改进</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-core=\"1\" data-hay=\"How AI Is Rewriting the Power Law of Venture Capital power law death of the middle TPPI vintage ARR LBO\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-a16z-ai-让风投的幂律变得更极端-而不是更温和/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7b2f032532c3a865-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">49:23</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">a16z</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>AI 让风投的幂律变得更极端，而不是更温和</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">3000 家风投里只有 20 家连续二十年做到 3 倍净回报。AI 第一次让钱能直接换成算力、算力直接变成产品优势，幂律因此更陡，而非更平。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">风险投资</span><span class=\"tag\">AI 配置</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-core=\"1\" data-hay=\"Coinbase’s Everything Exchange: Agentic Finance, Stablecoins, and Tokenization with CEO Brian Armstrong Everything Exchange X402 agentic finance epigenetic reprogramming\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-nopriors-给-ai-代理开户-信用卡手续费撑不起机器经济/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/4f9f8b9697bf1eed-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"N\"><span class=\"dur\">45:09</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">No Priors</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>给 AI 代理开户：信用卡手续费撑不起机器经济</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Coinbase 想让每个 AI 代理都有自己的账户：76% 的机器支付在 30 美分以下，而信用卡的最低手续费恰好就是 30 美分——旧支付轨道撑不起机器经济。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">加密支付</span><span class=\"tag\">AI 代理</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-core=\"1\" data-hay=\"The Finances of Marriage | Rational Reminder 426 tight wad spendthrift unconflicted consumer financial infidelity prenup\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-rationalreminder-结婚前先做花钱测试-紧手和挥霍者互相吸引-也更容易离婚/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/ad3115003cac32ae-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:19:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Rational Reminder</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>结婚前先做花钱测试：紧手和挥霍者互相吸引，也更容易离婚</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">研究把花钱的人分成紧手和挥霍者，两端的人更容易互相吸引，但婚后金钱冲突更多、婚姻满意度更低；婚礼花得越多，离婚风险反而越高。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">个人财务</span><span class=\"tag\">婚姻</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-core=\"1\" data-hay=\"The Finances of Marriage | #426 tightwad spendthrift anticipatory pain of paying financial infidelity unconflicted consumer\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-rationalreminder-婚礼花得越多离婚率越高-最省的那批人反而最稳/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/0e52c937f0d183da-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:08:25</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Rational Reminder</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>婚礼花得越多离婚率越高，最省的那批人反而最稳</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">研究显示婚礼花费越低离婚率越低，低于一千美元的那批人离婚率最低；而订婚戒指花得越多，男性离婚风险越高。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">婚姻财务</span><span class=\"tag\">消费心理</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The Predatory Industry Behind MLB’s Dominican Superstar Pipeline early agreement international draft signing bonus Dominican Summer League\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-papertrail-mlb-在多米尼加建了棒球城堡-也养出了放贷人/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/ed1b4a79f40f86fd-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">44:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Paper Trail</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>MLB 在多米尼加建了棒球城堡，也养出了放贷人</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">MLB 每年在多米尼加投入高达 4 亿美元，却没有选秀、允许 16 岁前私下签约，于是催生了一个向球员家庭放高利贷的影子产业，而 David Ortiz 被指是其中一环。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>9</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">体育产业</span><span class=\"tag\">调查报道</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Where Have The Insects Gone?? With Dr. Jessica Ware colony collapse disorder Varroa mite neonicotinoid pollinator garden oothika spiracles\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-sciencevs-昆虫正在消失-但杀虫剂不是最大凶手/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/632ea71d96602758-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">45:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Science Vs</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>昆虫正在消失，但杀虫剂不是最大凶手</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">昆虫数量下降被反复质疑夸大，但全球数据仍在指向同一方向；真正被低估的凶手不是农业，而是普通人随手买来用的杀虫剂。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">生态</span><span class=\"tag\">昆虫</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"E909.我们给残障人写「爽文」戏剧，把健全人写成弱势群体 原罪人 镜面人 口述影像\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-cn907a40-残障剧团让健全人当被歧视的少数-不是要你同情/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b8c6d4c5deab1aa2-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"故\"><span class=\"dur\">41:16</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">故事FM</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>残障剧团让健全人当被歧视的少数，不是要你同情</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">妖妖把社会关系整个调转过来：核战后多数人成了改造人，少数没改造的健全人成了原罪人，要争取权利的反倒是他们。这不是诉苦，是给残障人写的爽文。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">残障</span><span class=\"tag\">戏剧</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Archive: Plato&#x27;s Republic Thrasymachus the Forms the cave the ring of Gyges tripartite soul demagogue\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-inourtime-柏拉图理想国-民主离暴政只差一个煽动家/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b92ca842f2a04535-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">50:46</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">In Our Time</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>柏拉图理想国：民主离暴政只差一个煽动家</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">柏拉图认为民主制内部就埋着滑向暴政的通道，被野心家利用只是时间问题；而正义不是外在行为，是灵魂内部的秩序。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">哲学</span><span class=\"tag\">政治哲学</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Essentials: Genes &amp; the Inheritance of Memories Across Generations | Dr. Oded Rechavi Weismann barrier C. elegans small RNAs RNA interference epigenetic reprogramming\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-huberman-获得性遗传在线虫已被证实-人类还没有证据/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/8f8083a6d5296169-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"H\"><span class=\"dur\">35:38</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Huberman Lab</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>获得性遗传在线虫已被证实，人类还没有证据</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">教科书用魏斯曼屏障解释为什么练出的肌肉传不下去；但在线虫里，敲掉后代自己造小 RNA 的能力，它们仍能抵抗父母遇过的病毒，只改大脑里的 RNA 就能改变三代后的行为。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">表观遗传</span><span class=\"tag\">线虫</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Robert A. Wilson, &quot;Kin Matters: Relational Beings in the Fragile Sciences&quot; (Oxford UP, 2026) progenerative view Westermark hypothesis separatism extended cognition homeostatic property cluster disciplinary groove\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-nbphilosophy-亲属关系不是文化发明-而是生殖事实的文化延展/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/1c8789e8a81bb90f-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"N\"><span class=\"dur\">1:06:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">New Books in Philosophy</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>亲属关系不是文化发明，而是生殖事实的文化延展</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">人类学家说亲属关系纯属文化建构，哲学家却指出：女性先怀孕后生育这类生殖事实跨文化通用，亲属制度是对它们的文化延展，连乱伦回避也不是人类独有。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>10</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">人类学</span><span class=\"tag\">亲属关系</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-core=\"1\" data-hay=\"The Rise of Organized Retail Crime at Big Box Stores shrink ORC (organized retail crime) boosters fence INFORM Act edge analytics\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-oddlots-偷来的货能卖到原价七八折-零售盗窃已经产业化/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">52:39</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>偷来的货能卖到原价七八折，零售盗窃已经产业化</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">被盗商品要经过两层手：boosters 被招募进店偷货，fence 负责清洗标识和转售，之后挂上二手平台。联网的赃物能卖到原价七八折，T 恤和除臭剂只剩三成多。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">零售损耗</span><span class=\"tag\">有组织零售犯罪</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"How baseball got its beat walk-up song seventh inning stretch Tin Pan Alley closer\" href=\"/podcast/p/2026-09-10-throughline-棒球场的音乐不是伴奏-是球迷抢回比赛的方式/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2f35a52e32ee13fa-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">32:03</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Throughline</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0910</span></div>\n<h2>棒球场的音乐不是伴奏，是球迷抢回比赛的方式</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">棒球官方史学家嫌球场音乐太吵，但正是球迷齐唱 Hey Hey Goodbye 把客队投手唱到手软——音乐让观众从看客变成比赛的一部分。</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> 要点</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> 金句</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">棒球</span><span class=\"tag\">现场体验</span>\n</div></div></a>"]